  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 5.City Gate
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: City Gate
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.50905, y: 35.89612}
  firstPartInfo: "I\u2019m interested in the bigger picture of poverty in Malta at
    the time. Perhaps it might help to get a different perspective. Let me follow
    in someone else\u2019s footsteps for a while..  Five years before Isidoro\u2019s
    arrest, Teresa Dimech paced anxiously, working up the courage to enter the main
    street of the city, through a gate that looked very different from the city\u2019s
    entranceway today. She was here to lodge her plea - not the first time that she
    would beg for her son\u2019s release. Her steps would eventually lead her to
    the Palace but for now, the Gozitan woman is overwhelmed by the city bustle.
    She has a <link=Image_3><u><color=blue>letter</link></u></color>, carefully prepared
    with the aid of a notary or clerk. Her letter explains: \u2018Your Petitioner
    having lately had the misfortune of losing her Husband, was consequently thrown
    into the greatest state of poverty, by living as she has done since her marriage,
    in the village of Zebbug, Gozo, where she can scarcely obtain the common necessaries
    of life, and to add to her distressing case, she has to provide for her young,
    and helpless family which consists of 5 in number.\u2019 "
  secondPartInfo: "Her son, Giuseppe Dimech, had been tried by the <link=Image_4a><u><color=blue>Court
    of Special Commission</link></u></color>, for the crime of Homicide, and was
    serving a \u2018sentence of imprisonment for 20 years, with hard labour\u2019.
    She desperately hopes her letter is deferential and formal enough to win a favourable
    response. Sadly, the Chief Secretary to the Governor would disagree, finding
    that: \u2018The case of this man has been repeatedly considered. There is no
    additional reason stated here that might, in my opinion, justify a <link=Image_5><u><color=blue>pardon</link></u></color>
    for the present.\u2019  I shall follow Teresa Dimech down Valletta\u2019s main
    thoroughfare - the street the British renamed Kingsway - until I arrive at the
    place where her son\u2019s case, and Isidoro Mifsud\u2019s, would have been heard
    - a place I am still likely to meet judges to this day.  "
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Poverty
  hintOfPOI: "It\u2019s easy! Just follow the lawyers with their suits and briefcases
    as they rush in for a day\u2019s work."
  solutionOfPOI: 'The building might have changed, but the location is still the
    same: I need to go to the Courts of Justice.'
